================================================================================
Prompt: causal_validate.j2
Service Step: VALIDATE_CAUSAL (Causal Verification)
Function Summary: Perform in-depth causal chain audit on chapter body text, output causal verification report (supports full/recheck modes).
Upstream Input:
  - causal_link: Causal chain anchor from BRIDGE_CHAPTER
  - chapter_bridge: Bridge contract from BRIDGE_CHAPTER
  - chapter_number: Chapter number
  - character_notes: Character notes
  - previous_chapter_ending: Ending text from previous chapter Persist
  - chapter_text / numbered_chapter_text: Text to be verified
  - recheck_mode: Whether it is recheck mode
  - prior_issues: Previous round issue list
  - repaired_issue_types: Issue types involved in this repair
  - must_resolve_summaries: Blocking archive issues that must be resolved
  - must_resolve_issue_ids: Issue IDs that must be rechecked
Downstream Output:
  - JSON: Causal verification result, output contract injected by Builder
  - Downstream Consumer: CausalRepairStep (for causal repair)
Consumption Chain Priority: P0 (event occurring out of nowhere/causal contradiction) > P1 (missing decision motivation/insufficient transition setup)
              > P2 (suspense management explicitly listed in causal_link)
Brief Example:
  Input: recheck_mode=true, prior_issues=[{"issue_type": "opening_causal_gap", "severity": "high"}]
  Output: {"causal_score": 9.0, "issues": []}
